1
00:01:37,040 --> 00:01:40,400
=Ren Yu=

2
00:01:40,400 --> 00:01:43,000
(Adapted from Lei Mi's novel Ren Yu)

3
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:45,960
=Episode 7=

4
00:01:49,640 --> 00:01:50,560
Su Lin's home number.

5
00:01:53,079 --> 00:01:54,040
Thank you, Mr. Zhou.

6
00:01:54,359 --> 00:01:54,799
No problem.

7
00:01:59,719 --> 00:02:00,200
Jiang Ting.

8
00:02:01,519 --> 00:02:03,159
I've been meaning to warn you.

9
00:02:03,560 --> 00:02:05,359
Stay away from Ma Na.

10
00:02:06,120 --> 00:02:08,479
Avoid confronting her directly.

11
00:02:09,360 --> 00:02:10,400
As a teacher,

12
00:02:11,560 --> 00:02:12,560
I shouldn't say this.

13
00:02:13,439 --> 00:02:15,560
But we don't live in a fairy tale.

14
00:02:16,479 --> 00:02:17,479
You're a smart girl.

15
00:02:18,120 --> 00:02:19,000
You know what I mean.

16
00:02:21,159 --> 00:02:21,759
Thank you.

17
00:02:23,360 --> 00:02:23,800
Hey!

18
00:02:25,759 --> 00:02:26,400
Hurry home.

19
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:30,360
Young man.

20
00:02:31,800 --> 00:02:32,479
Bike trouble?

21
00:02:32,759 --> 00:02:33,719
Looks like the chain

22
00:02:34,039 --> 00:02:34,879
came off.

23
00:02:34,879 --> 00:02:35,879
Repair stand's outside.

24
00:02:35,960 --> 00:02:36,680
I'll carry it over.

25
00:02:37,639 --> 00:02:38,400
Sorry for the trouble.

26
00:02:38,439 --> 00:02:38,919
No trouble.

27
00:02:39,520 --> 00:02:40,240
Hurry home.

28
00:02:41,360 --> 00:02:42,240
Bye, Mr. Zhou.

29
00:02:52,520 --> 00:02:54,400
Your theory hinges on one thing.

30
00:02:54,479 --> 00:02:55,120
You know that?

31
00:02:55,520 --> 00:02:57,800
We need confirmed crime scenes.

32
00:02:58,439 --> 00:02:59,719
Captain, hear me out.

33
00:02:59,840 --> 00:03:00,199
Go ahead.

34
00:03:00,520 --> 00:03:01,560
Let me walk you through it.

35
00:03:02,039 --> 00:03:02,960
We now know

36
00:03:03,199 --> 00:03:05,240
the three victims'

37
00:03:05,560 --> 00:03:06,599
daily routines,

38
00:03:06,759 --> 00:03:07,639
workplaces and homes,

39
00:03:08,080 --> 00:03:10,960
and where each left from that day.

40
00:03:11,960 --> 00:03:13,280
Take the first victim.

41
00:03:13,960 --> 00:03:15,719
She visited three places that day.

42
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:17,199
We inspect all three

43
00:03:17,199 --> 00:03:18,199
in person,

44
00:03:18,560 --> 00:03:20,520
then identify the likeliest crime scene.

45
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:22,120
You call that analysis?

46
00:03:22,800 --> 00:03:23,680
That's guessing.

47
00:03:25,759 --> 00:03:27,240
Fine. Get to work.

48
00:03:27,439 --> 00:03:27,840
Let's do it.

49
00:04:32,720 --> 00:04:33,360
Back to business.

50
00:04:33,800 --> 00:04:35,279
Copy this.

51
00:04:35,720 --> 00:04:36,439
(Police)
One each.

52
00:04:37,240 --> 00:04:37,920
Keep canvassing.

53
00:04:38,040 --> 00:04:38,319
Got it.

54
00:04:38,680 --> 00:04:39,120
Thanks.

55
00:04:39,160 --> 00:04:39,600
Get in.

56
00:04:39,680 --> 00:04:40,279
Come on, get in.

57
00:04:40,839 --> 00:04:41,720
- See you.
- Stay safe.

58
00:04:41,800 --> 00:04:42,319
Be careful.

59
00:04:42,399 --> 00:04:42,839
See you.

60
00:04:43,839 --> 00:04:44,399
Slow down.

61
00:04:44,440 --> 00:04:45,920
(Police)

62
00:04:54,399 --> 00:04:54,920
Come on.

63
00:04:54,959 --> 00:04:56,160
What's wrong with a hug?

64
00:04:56,160 --> 00:04:57,160
I just want to hold you.

65
00:07:20,480 --> 00:07:20,959
Hello?

66
00:07:24,160 --> 00:07:24,759
Hello?

67
00:07:27,800 --> 00:07:28,360
Lin?

68
00:07:29,399 --> 00:07:30,160
Is that you?

69
00:07:31,759 --> 00:07:33,439
Lin, when are you coming back?

70
00:07:34,759 --> 00:07:36,120
I know I was wrong.

71
00:07:36,160 --> 00:07:37,360
Please don't abandon me.

72
00:07:37,879 --> 00:07:39,319
(Su Lin still hasn't come home?)

73
00:07:40,199 --> 00:07:41,720
Who told you to answer?

74
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:44,720
Hello? Who is this?

75
00:07:46,600 --> 00:07:47,639
Hello? Who do you want?

76
00:07:49,279 --> 00:07:49,839
Hello?

77
00:07:54,079 --> 00:07:54,800
Who called?

78
00:07:55,319 --> 00:07:56,199
A woman.

79
00:07:56,240 --> 00:07:58,439
She asked if Lin was still gone.

80
00:08:28,639 --> 00:08:30,079
If that happens again,

81
00:08:31,480 --> 00:08:33,399
let me answer it. Got it?

82
00:08:34,240 --> 00:08:34,919
Mom.

83
00:08:35,200 --> 00:08:36,679
Where did Lin really go?

84
00:08:39,720 --> 00:08:40,639
I already told you.

85
00:08:40,679 --> 00:08:41,360
Your sister

86
00:08:42,639 --> 00:08:43,639
went away for school.

87
00:08:43,799 --> 00:08:44,480
Stop asking.

88
00:08:46,679 --> 00:08:47,840
Go do your homework.

89
00:08:55,679 --> 00:08:56,360
Hello?

90
00:08:59,600 --> 00:09:00,240
One moment.

91
00:09:04,720 --> 00:09:06,080
Door 108, Lei Mi.

92
00:09:06,159 --> 00:09:07,039
Phone call.

93
00:09:34,320 --> 00:09:35,720
We're here.

94
00:09:37,639 --> 00:09:38,080
Oh, right.

95
00:09:39,240 --> 00:09:40,480
Any movement lately?

96
00:09:40,759 --> 00:09:41,919
He's normal during the day,

97
00:09:42,759 --> 00:09:44,320
but roams around at night.

98
00:09:44,519 --> 00:09:46,000
He's probably looking for his daughter.

99
00:09:47,879 --> 00:09:49,039
He also bought dinner

100
00:09:49,159 --> 00:09:50,840
for a cabbie friend.

101
00:09:55,960 --> 00:09:56,679
Check this out.

102
00:09:58,240 --> 00:09:59,080
He went to a print shop

103
00:09:59,320 --> 00:10:00,840
and printed these missing-person flyers.

104
00:10:01,240 --> 00:10:02,240
(Missing Person)
None posted.

105
00:10:02,399 --> 00:10:03,240
He threw them all away.

106
00:10:12,679 --> 00:10:13,120
Okay.

107
00:10:13,360 --> 00:10:14,519
Keep a closer eye on him.

108
00:10:23,519 --> 00:10:24,039
Mom.

109
00:10:24,039 --> 00:10:25,039
Yeah?

110
00:10:26,919 --> 00:10:28,120
If I went missing,

111
00:10:29,200 --> 00:10:30,360
would you look for me?

112
00:10:31,600 --> 00:10:32,720
Don't say that.

113
00:10:33,080 --> 00:10:34,559
Knock on wood. Now.

114
00:10:34,879 --> 00:10:35,759
What's gotten into you?

115
00:10:35,840 --> 00:10:37,320
Why say something so awful?

116
00:10:39,840 --> 00:10:41,559
I was just thinking...

117
00:10:41,639 --> 00:10:42,879
Think about anything else.

118
00:10:43,559 --> 00:10:44,440
Not that.

119
00:10:45,320 --> 00:10:46,360
How would you go missing?

120
00:10:47,120 --> 00:10:47,799
Besides,

121
00:10:48,840 --> 00:10:49,600
if you did,

122
00:10:49,879 --> 00:10:51,559
I'd search the whole world for you.

123
00:10:52,200 --> 00:10:52,919
Don't think that way.

124
00:10:55,679 --> 00:10:57,399
Has something been troubling you?

125
00:10:59,840 --> 00:11:00,480
No.

126
00:11:04,159 --> 00:11:06,799
I just feel

127
00:11:08,759 --> 00:11:10,240
stressful lately.

128
00:11:11,240 --> 00:11:11,799
It's okay.

129
00:11:37,200 --> 00:11:38,440
(Mind your own business.)

130
00:11:42,559 --> 00:11:44,480
Stay away from Ma Na.

131
00:11:44,840 --> 00:11:47,120
Avoid confronting her directly.

132
00:12:49,320 --> 00:12:52,200
(Is there really no way out?)

133
00:13:07,799 --> 00:13:09,000
(I have no strength left.)

134
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:14,279
(Let it all end.)

135
00:13:25,720 --> 00:13:26,320
What is it?

136
00:13:30,720 --> 00:13:31,440
(Admissions Guide)
Where'd this come from?

137
00:13:36,080 --> 00:13:36,960
You searched my drawer?

138
00:13:37,399 --> 00:13:39,360
(Admissions Guide)
Think carefully before you answer.

139
00:13:41,759 --> 00:13:42,440
Dad gave it to me.

140
00:13:42,640 --> 00:13:45,240
(Admissions Guide)

141
00:13:49,840 --> 00:13:50,720
Can you not pick up

142
00:13:50,720 --> 00:13:51,679
your dad's bad habits?

143
00:13:51,679 --> 00:13:53,200
(Northern Normal University)

144
00:13:54,360 --> 00:13:55,679
Why did you bookmark this?

145
00:13:57,600 --> 00:13:59,720
Why did he give you this?

146
00:14:01,679 --> 00:14:03,440
He wants me to study in Beijing.

147
00:14:04,000 --> 00:14:05,279
He says I'll have a better future.

148
00:14:07,000 --> 00:14:07,840
What do you think?

149
00:14:10,240 --> 00:14:11,279
I haven't thought about it.

150
00:14:24,000 --> 00:14:24,759
I'll do it.

151
00:14:24,840 --> 00:14:25,559
Let me.

152
00:14:28,440 --> 00:14:31,240
Your high school exam score was low.

153
00:14:32,000 --> 00:14:33,200
I couldn't help you,

154
00:14:33,600 --> 00:14:34,559
and Dad gave us nothing.

155
00:14:35,000 --> 00:14:36,000
We couldn't pay that fee.

156
00:14:36,919 --> 00:14:37,639
That meant

157
00:14:39,039 --> 00:14:40,120
you went to vocational school.

158
00:14:42,919 --> 00:14:44,080
At the time, I thought

159
00:14:45,000 --> 00:14:46,960
you could stay close to me

160
00:14:48,120 --> 00:14:50,159
and find work here someday.

161
00:14:51,159 --> 00:14:54,159
But if you truly want Beijing,

162
00:14:54,919 --> 00:14:55,840
that's okay too.

163
00:14:57,120 --> 00:14:58,240
I'll go with you.

164
00:14:59,200 --> 00:15:01,720
I'll rent a place near your school,

165
00:15:02,000 --> 00:15:03,600
cook for you, and do your laundry.

166
00:15:04,919 --> 00:15:06,279
I can find another job.

167
00:15:07,279 --> 00:15:09,799
It'll be easier if we're together,

168
00:15:10,000 --> 00:15:10,639
and I won't worry.

169
00:15:10,679 --> 00:15:11,840
I'm not going to Beijing.

170
00:15:12,000 --> 00:15:13,039
What's wrong with Beijing?

171
00:15:13,360 --> 00:15:14,480
It's a great place.

172
00:15:14,519 --> 00:15:16,000
I'm not stopping you.

173
00:15:17,720 --> 00:15:19,559
I'll support whatever you choose.

174
00:15:20,320 --> 00:15:23,399
But if you have plans,

175
00:15:24,000 --> 00:15:25,080
you need to tell me.

176
00:15:25,399 --> 00:15:26,000
You're young.

177
00:15:26,080 --> 00:15:27,039
You can't decide alone.

178
00:15:27,240 --> 00:15:29,120
I didn't tell you so you wouldn't worry.

179
00:15:29,279 --> 00:15:30,960
Not telling me makes me worry more.

180
00:15:34,720 --> 00:15:37,320
Those dark, sparkling eyes

181
00:15:37,600 --> 00:15:39,720
are your smiling face.

182
00:15:44,559 --> 00:15:45,080
What is it?

183
00:15:45,600 --> 00:15:46,120
Nothing.

184
00:15:48,200 --> 00:15:48,720
It's nothing.

185
00:15:50,080 --> 00:15:50,759
What happened?

186
00:15:51,039 --> 00:15:51,919
- Nothing.
- Let me see.

187
00:15:59,679 --> 00:16:00,799
Leave it. She's gone too far.

188
00:16:00,960 --> 00:16:01,600
Don't get mad.

189
00:16:01,600 --> 00:16:02,399
Get up. Come on.

190
00:16:05,600 --> 00:16:06,200
Cute, right?

191
00:16:06,399 --> 00:16:07,240
It's for Han Mei.

192
00:16:07,600 --> 00:16:08,840
She treats you well.

193
00:16:09,200 --> 00:16:10,519
Why are you always mean to her?

194
00:16:10,759 --> 00:16:11,960
I've put up with you long enough.

195
00:16:13,399 --> 00:16:14,440
I'm good to her too.

196
00:16:15,000 --> 00:16:16,519
Didn't I just give her a gift?

197
00:16:16,759 --> 00:16:17,960
If you're upset, take it out on me.

198
00:16:18,000 --> 00:16:19,360
Stop giving her trouble.

199
00:16:22,879 --> 00:16:24,080
What a loving couple.

200
00:16:28,120 --> 00:16:29,559
Look at Mom's picture

201
00:16:29,600 --> 00:16:30,559
and say that again.

202
00:16:30,720 --> 00:16:32,279
Stop bringing up the past.

203
00:16:32,440 --> 00:16:34,120
Do you remember what today is?

204
00:16:34,200 --> 00:16:35,000
What is it?

205
00:16:35,240 --> 00:16:36,759
It's the anniversary of Mom's death.

206
00:16:50,399 --> 00:16:52,039
You really forgot everything.

207
00:17:06,519 --> 00:17:07,920
I'm sorry, Na.

208
00:17:09,960 --> 00:17:11,319
I did forget.

209
00:17:14,920 --> 00:17:15,559
Na.

210
00:17:16,480 --> 00:17:19,440
But we have to move forward.

211
00:17:19,720 --> 00:17:20,799
I can't.

212
00:17:22,240 --> 00:17:24,160
Mom's blood runs through me.

213
00:17:24,920 --> 00:17:25,640
Not you.

214
00:17:26,119 --> 00:17:27,240
You move on.

215
00:17:31,039 --> 00:17:32,480
You already have, haven't you?

216
00:17:36,359 --> 00:17:37,119
As a father,

217
00:17:38,160 --> 00:17:39,359
I've failed you.

218
00:17:40,480 --> 00:17:41,559
All your life,

219
00:17:43,079 --> 00:17:45,039
I never made time for you.

220
00:17:45,759 --> 00:17:47,480
I deprived you of so much.

221
00:17:50,119 --> 00:17:51,039
Sometimes,

222
00:17:51,079 --> 00:17:52,240
I don't want to spoil you.

223
00:17:53,200 --> 00:17:54,599
But I can't help it.

224
00:17:55,680 --> 00:17:57,079
You're not only my daughter.

225
00:17:58,759 --> 00:18:00,400
You're your mother's daughter too.

226
00:18:03,079 --> 00:18:03,920
You should know,

227
00:18:05,519 --> 00:18:07,640
before you came into this world,

228
00:18:08,839 --> 00:18:10,680
she mattered most to me.

229
00:18:14,960 --> 00:18:16,839
But now, the one who matters most

230
00:18:17,799 --> 00:18:18,640
isn't Mom,

231
00:18:19,720 --> 00:18:20,839
or me, is it?

232
00:18:22,319 --> 00:18:23,359
To me,

233
00:18:23,400 --> 00:18:24,720
you'll always matter most.

234
00:18:26,079 --> 00:18:28,200
No one could ever replace you.

235
00:18:28,519 --> 00:18:30,240
Then why send me abroad?

236
00:18:31,039 --> 00:18:32,000
You're sick of me.

237
00:18:32,000 --> 00:18:33,079
You think I'm a burden.

238
00:18:33,119 --> 00:18:34,920
You want a family with Han Mei.

239
00:18:35,319 --> 00:18:36,599
Mei and I

240
00:18:36,640 --> 00:18:38,839
have never thought that.

241
00:18:39,359 --> 00:18:40,160
I'm sending you abroad

242
00:18:40,200 --> 00:18:42,240
to give you a better education

243
00:18:42,519 --> 00:18:44,519
and a better life.

244
00:18:46,039 --> 00:18:46,880
I don't want to go.

245
00:18:47,680 --> 00:18:49,160
Why not?

246
00:18:49,240 --> 00:18:50,240
I said I don't want to!

247
00:18:50,319 --> 00:18:51,599
Why are you trying to get rid of me?

248
00:18:53,079 --> 00:18:53,720
Na.

249
00:18:55,160 --> 00:18:57,079
I'd never want to send you away.

250
00:18:58,039 --> 00:18:59,359
This is for your own good.

251
00:19:00,160 --> 00:19:02,039
I'd do anything for you.

252
00:19:02,640 --> 00:19:04,640
Can you give me my old life back?

253
00:19:19,559 --> 00:19:20,480
Su.

254
00:19:22,680 --> 00:19:23,680
Your dad's home.

255
00:19:35,440 --> 00:19:36,119
Doing homework?

256
00:19:38,000 --> 00:19:39,039
Any word

257
00:19:39,559 --> 00:19:40,880
from Ma Dongchen?

258
00:19:43,279 --> 00:19:43,759
Nothing.

259
00:19:49,960 --> 00:19:51,599
You're home late every night.

260
00:19:53,440 --> 00:19:55,359
If I don't work, will you feed us?

261
00:20:08,000 --> 00:20:09,920
I want to run something by you.

262
00:20:10,440 --> 00:20:11,880
Want me to drink from the bottle?

263
00:20:19,039 --> 00:20:21,039
My boss at the laundromat

264
00:20:21,119 --> 00:20:22,720
is from Yancheng.

265
00:20:22,920 --> 00:20:24,319
Maybe we could ask her

266
00:20:24,480 --> 00:20:26,039
to look into it for us.

267
00:20:26,599 --> 00:20:28,440
Yancheng?

268
00:20:29,480 --> 00:20:31,519
Lin wouldn't chase some celebrity there.

269
00:20:32,119 --> 00:20:34,480
I don't believe that either.

270
00:20:34,920 --> 00:20:37,480
But we just learned about the tapes.

271
00:20:37,480 --> 00:20:38,400
So I thought,

272
00:20:39,160 --> 00:20:40,599
maybe it's possible.

273
00:20:40,599 --> 00:20:41,319
Besides,

274
00:20:41,920 --> 00:20:43,319
we don't know

275
00:20:43,359 --> 00:20:44,880
what kids are into these days.

276
00:20:45,240 --> 00:20:46,240
Yancheng is so far away.

277
00:20:46,359 --> 00:20:47,599
We don't know anyone there.

278
00:20:48,000 --> 00:20:48,640
Besides,

279
00:20:49,279 --> 00:20:51,079
who'd care enough to help you?

280
00:20:51,480 --> 00:20:53,680
You spend all day dreaming up nonsense.

281
00:20:55,720 --> 00:20:58,200
Then we'll look into it ourselves.

282
00:21:05,480 --> 00:21:06,240
Honey.

283
00:21:08,839 --> 00:21:09,680
Honey.

284
00:21:11,200 --> 00:21:14,079
What if we put up missing-person flyers?

285
00:21:15,559 --> 00:21:16,480
You think you're so smart.

286
00:21:17,519 --> 00:21:19,319
Like I never thought of that.

287
00:21:20,960 --> 00:21:21,799
You know nothing.

288
00:21:21,839 --> 00:21:22,640
Go to bed.

289
00:21:32,520 --> 00:21:33,800
(Gaolianghong)

290
00:21:37,799 --> 00:21:39,400
All you do is drink.

291
00:21:40,559 --> 00:21:41,880
How can you still drink?

292
00:21:42,240 --> 00:21:44,039
Do you even care?

293
00:21:44,799 --> 00:21:46,440
I don't care?

294
00:21:47,039 --> 00:21:48,680
I work myself to death every day.

295
00:21:48,759 --> 00:21:50,359
I do it for this family!

296
00:21:51,720 --> 00:21:53,279
If I don't have a drink,

297
00:21:53,480 --> 00:21:54,880
I can't close my eyes.

298
00:21:55,000 --> 00:21:56,119
I can't sleep.

299
00:21:56,240 --> 00:21:58,160
Then go look instead of sleeping!

300
00:21:58,960 --> 00:22:00,559
Why do you think

301
00:22:00,599 --> 00:22:01,720
I'm home so late every night?

302
00:22:02,440 --> 00:22:03,920
I've been looking for our girl.

303
00:22:04,680 --> 00:22:05,480
Don't you know

304
00:22:05,759 --> 00:22:07,240
that Ma guy is watching us?

305
00:22:07,400 --> 00:22:09,240
I have to search in secret.

306
00:22:09,880 --> 00:22:10,960
What power do we have

307
00:22:11,000 --> 00:22:12,400
to take him on directly?

308
00:22:13,079 --> 00:22:14,160
I can't do it.

309
00:22:14,839 --> 00:22:16,759
Neither can this family.

310
00:23:13,760 --> 00:23:14,460
Alas.

311
00:23:16,800 --> 00:23:17,559
What do you want?

312
00:23:18,400 --> 00:23:18,920
Jiang Ting.

313
00:23:19,279 --> 00:23:20,680
Aren't you looking for Su Lin?

314
00:23:21,160 --> 00:23:21,599
Come on.

315
00:23:21,880 --> 00:23:22,839
We'll take you to her.

316
00:23:23,039 --> 00:23:23,519
Come on.

317
00:23:26,680 --> 00:23:28,359
What? Are you scared?

318
00:23:29,200 --> 00:23:30,440
Don't be.

319
00:23:30,519 --> 00:23:32,279
We're really taking you to Su Lin.

320
00:23:32,319 --> 00:23:32,599
Right.

321
00:23:32,680 --> 00:23:33,640
This is your only chance.

322
00:23:33,880 --> 00:23:34,440
Let's go.

323
00:24:03,559 --> 00:24:04,559
Let go of me!

324
00:24:04,559 --> 00:24:05,279
You're not leaving.

325
00:24:05,279 --> 00:24:05,920
Let go!

326
00:24:06,720 --> 00:24:07,599
Let go!

327
00:24:09,599 --> 00:24:10,440
I don't want to go!

328
00:24:10,960 --> 00:24:11,680
Get in there!

329
00:24:13,920 --> 00:24:14,640
No! No!

330
00:24:15,200 --> 00:24:15,720
No!

331
00:24:16,119 --> 00:24:16,920
What are you doing?

332
00:24:17,359 --> 00:24:18,480
Let me out!

333
00:24:19,079 --> 00:24:20,279
Let me out!

334
00:24:20,319 --> 00:24:21,599
What are you doing?

335
00:24:22,519 --> 00:24:24,960
Mom will panic when she can't find me!

336
00:24:25,400 --> 00:24:26,400
Let me out!

337
00:24:26,880 --> 00:24:28,000
Let me out!

338
00:24:28,480 --> 00:24:29,920
Ma Na, please!

339
00:24:29,920 --> 00:24:31,559
Please let me out!

340
00:24:32,720 --> 00:24:33,920
I'm begging you!

341
00:24:34,000 --> 00:24:35,559
Please, I'm begging you!

342
00:24:35,799 --> 00:24:38,240
Let me out!

343
00:24:38,559 --> 00:24:39,599
Let me out!

344
00:24:41,640 --> 00:24:42,720
Please!

345
00:24:42,759 --> 00:24:44,440
I'm begging you!

346
00:24:45,880 --> 00:24:47,200
Is anyone there?

347
00:24:56,279 --> 00:24:58,880
Why are you doing this to me?

348
00:25:00,920 --> 00:25:02,279
Why?

349
00:28:27,280 --> 00:28:29,120
(I hate school.)

350
00:28:29,120 --> 00:28:31,400
(Wang Dong was here.)

351
00:28:38,160 --> 00:28:39,880
(I want to be with him forever.)

352
00:28:40,839 --> 00:28:42,039
(Restore our land.)

353
00:28:42,440 --> 00:28:43,880
(I hope I hit the jackpot.)

354
00:28:45,519 --> 00:28:47,119
(I want to be a dancer.)

355
00:28:48,599 --> 00:28:50,519
(I want to see Andy Lau in concert.)

356
00:28:51,680 --> 00:28:53,559
(I hate school.)

357
00:28:56,119 --> 00:28:58,400
(I wish it stayed at 20°C forever.)

358
00:28:58,960 --> 00:29:00,880
(Then the crops wouldn't grow.)

359
00:29:01,319 --> 00:29:02,880
(I wish all the boys in my class)

360
00:29:02,880 --> 00:29:04,400
(would turn into girls.)

361
00:29:05,160 --> 00:29:06,160
(I wish every girl in class)

362
00:29:06,160 --> 00:29:07,359
(would become one of the guys.)

363
00:29:08,240 --> 00:29:10,240
(I want Grandma to stay healthy.)

364
00:29:11,640 --> 00:29:13,920
(I want Mom and Dad to stop fighting.)

365
00:29:13,920 --> 00:29:15,840
♪The dust with nowhere to escape♪

366
00:29:17,640 --> 00:29:21,080
♪Is me♪

367
00:29:21,200 --> 00:29:24,040
♪Never loud, never surging♪

368
00:29:24,040 --> 00:29:29,560
♪I gather my worries and build a wall♪

369
00:29:30,440 --> 00:29:35,600
♪Around me♪

370
00:29:35,600 --> 00:29:38,500
♪By my pillow, I hear♪

371
00:29:38,500 --> 00:29:43,170
♪A dark fairy tale♪

372
00:29:43,171 --> 00:29:47,840
♪A dark fairy tale♪

373
00:29:47,840 --> 00:29:52,440
Keep moving. Don't stop.

374
00:29:52,440 --> 00:29:58,080
♪A thousand flowers bloom♪

375
00:29:59,720 --> 00:30:06,040
♪From the tower, I gaze afar♪

376
00:30:06,040 --> 00:30:12,520
♪How radiant♪

377
00:30:13,120 --> 00:30:19,560
♪Now I stand with myself♪

378
00:30:19,560 --> 00:30:23,940
♪Each becomes the other's shore♪

379
00:30:23,941 --> 00:30:28,320
♪Each becomes the other's shore♪

380
00:30:54,560 --> 00:30:57,740
♪By my pillow, I hear♪

381
00:30:57,740 --> 00:31:04,538
♪A dark fairy tale♪

382
00:31:04,538 --> 00:31:06,800
(Don't help them bury the light.)

383
00:31:07,800 --> 00:31:11,000
♪One burst of pain♪

384
00:31:11,000 --> 00:31:17,880
♪A thousand flowers bloom♪

385
00:31:35,279 --> 00:31:36,400
Jiang Ting.

386
00:31:37,400 --> 00:31:38,640
You can do this.

387
00:31:38,640 --> 00:31:44,640
♪A thousand flowers bloom♪

388
00:31:45,080 --> 00:31:51,160
♪Like shattered spray♪

389
00:31:51,640 --> 00:31:58,200
♪Submerged♪

390
00:31:58,200 --> 00:32:02,140
♪The struggle inside the silence♪

391
00:32:02,141 --> 00:32:06,080
♪The struggle inside the silence♪

392
00:32:06,080 --> 00:32:09,320
♪Who can hear♪

393
00:32:12,200 --> 00:32:18,280
♪It♪

394
00:32:19,000 --> 00:32:22,480
(Hubei Provincial Education Bureau)

395
00:32:22,480 --> 00:32:23,119
Mr. Gu.

396
00:32:23,400 --> 00:32:23,960
(Moral Education Division)
Hello, Chief.

397
00:32:25,559 --> 00:32:26,160
Sorry I'm late.

398
00:32:26,160 --> 00:32:26,799
Deputy Chief Xu.

399
00:32:27,240 --> 00:32:28,359
Please, come in.

400
00:32:29,000 --> 00:32:30,000
Sorry for the trouble.

401
00:32:30,440 --> 00:32:31,200
Not at all.

402
00:32:31,759 --> 00:32:32,160
Have a seat.

403
00:32:39,160 --> 00:32:39,720
Mr. Gu.

404
00:32:40,160 --> 00:32:42,720
You called about a student?

405
00:32:43,000 --> 00:32:43,440
Yes.

406
00:32:44,640 --> 00:32:46,000
It rained hard a few days ago.

407
00:32:46,880 --> 00:32:48,000
I slipped on the road.

408
00:32:48,839 --> 00:32:50,400
A schoolgirl came by.

409
00:32:51,039 --> 00:32:52,279
She not only helped me up,

410
00:32:52,400 --> 00:32:53,480
but walked me home.

411
00:32:54,240 --> 00:32:56,000
I'd like to know her name

412
00:32:56,240 --> 00:32:57,359
and which school she attends.

413
00:32:57,680 --> 00:32:59,640
I want to write a letter praising her.

414
00:33:00,160 --> 00:33:02,720
But she wouldn't tell me anything.

415
00:33:03,240 --> 00:33:04,160
She just ran off.

416
00:33:04,400 --> 00:33:06,240
She did a good deed anonymously.

417
00:33:06,559 --> 00:33:07,720
She sounds like a good kid.

418
00:33:08,720 --> 00:33:09,720
How old was she?

419
00:33:09,799 --> 00:33:11,319
Do you know her school?

420
00:33:11,519 --> 00:33:12,240
High school age.

421
00:33:12,960 --> 00:33:14,319
Her uniform was blue and white,

422
00:33:14,839 --> 00:33:16,480
with a white stripe on the pants.

423
00:33:17,960 --> 00:33:19,400
Blue and white...

424
00:33:20,480 --> 00:33:21,000
Blue...

425
00:33:22,839 --> 00:33:23,880
Then she must be

426
00:33:24,119 --> 00:33:25,680
from Chaobei Vocational High School.

427
00:33:27,039 --> 00:33:28,400
What did she look like?

428
00:33:28,720 --> 00:33:30,400
Double eyelids, an oval face,

429
00:33:30,799 --> 00:33:33,240
and hair about this long.

430
00:33:34,599 --> 00:33:35,759
Wait here, Mr. Gu.

431
00:33:43,000 --> 00:33:43,480
It's me.

432
00:33:43,880 --> 00:33:46,039
Bring me the student records

433
00:33:46,079 --> 00:33:47,599
from Chaobei Vocational High School.

434
00:33:48,240 --> 00:33:49,920
Yes, all of them.

435
00:33:50,799 --> 00:33:51,599
One moment, Mr. Gu.

436
00:33:52,559 --> 00:33:53,359
Sorry for the trouble.

437
00:33:53,440 --> 00:33:54,240
Not at all.

438
00:33:58,079 --> 00:33:59,200
Here, have some water.

439
00:33:59,400 --> 00:33:59,799
Thanks.

440
00:34:03,920 --> 00:34:05,079
How's your father lately?

441
00:34:07,240 --> 00:34:09,519
One side is still paralyzed,

442
00:34:09,840 --> 00:34:11,000
but he eats and drinks fine.

443
00:34:12,280 --> 00:34:14,960
We're grateful for that much.

444
00:34:17,320 --> 00:34:18,039
Mr. Gu.

445
00:34:18,760 --> 00:34:21,079
If you hadn't driven the police car

446
00:34:21,519 --> 00:34:22,679
and taken Dad to the hospital,

447
00:34:24,000 --> 00:34:25,119
he probably would've...

448
00:34:28,599 --> 00:34:29,280
Thank you.

449
00:34:30,000 --> 00:34:32,280
The doctor said five minutes sooner

450
00:34:33,320 --> 00:34:36,000
and your father would've been fine.

451
00:34:37,639 --> 00:34:38,159
My fault.

452
00:34:39,119 --> 00:34:40,199
Please don't say that.

453
00:34:40,199 --> 00:34:40,719
Mr. Gu.

454
00:34:41,159 --> 00:34:42,920
Without you, he would've died.

455
00:34:44,519 --> 00:34:45,760
Chief, the files you requested.

456
00:34:46,039 --> 00:34:46,559
Put them here.

457
00:34:49,640 --> 00:34:50,560
(File Envelope)

458
00:34:50,599 --> 00:34:51,079
Mr. Gu.

459
00:34:51,920 --> 00:34:53,440
There are photos in every file.

460
00:34:53,840 --> 00:34:54,800
Take your time.

461
00:34:55,079 --> 00:34:55,880
I have work to do.

462
00:34:56,199 --> 00:34:57,079
I'll be back afterward.

463
00:34:57,400 --> 00:34:58,039
All right.

464
00:34:58,840 --> 00:35:03,599
The little mermaid drank
the magic draught.

465
00:35:04,159 --> 00:35:06,079
It seemed

466
00:35:06,119 --> 00:35:08,079
as if a two-edged sword

467
00:35:08,280 --> 00:35:10,880
went through her delicate body.

468
00:35:11,719 --> 00:35:14,039
She fell into a swoon

469
00:35:14,280 --> 00:35:16,440
and lay like one dead.

470
00:35:17,039 --> 00:35:18,239
When the sun rose over the sea,

471
00:35:18,239 --> 00:35:19,320
she awoke

472
00:35:19,760 --> 00:35:22,079
and felt a sharp pain.

473
00:35:22,639 --> 00:35:24,599
Before her stood

474
00:35:24,679 --> 00:35:28,159
the handsome young prince.

475
00:35:29,400 --> 00:35:32,280
He fixed his coal-black eyes upon her,

476
00:35:32,360 --> 00:35:34,760
and she cast down her own.

477
00:35:38,360 --> 00:35:38,840
Gather around.

478
00:35:45,239 --> 00:35:46,960
Less is more.

479
00:35:47,519 --> 00:35:48,880
Does anyone know what that means?

480
00:35:52,679 --> 00:35:53,559
Less is more.

481
00:35:55,360 --> 00:35:56,360
Great truths are simple.

482
00:35:57,079 --> 00:35:58,920
Less is more.

483
00:36:00,400 --> 00:36:01,800
The Little Mermaid is simple,

484
00:36:02,440 --> 00:36:03,119
innocent,

485
00:36:03,880 --> 00:36:05,079
and completely unadorned.

486
00:36:06,199 --> 00:36:09,159
Anything else would look wrong on her.

487
00:36:09,559 --> 00:36:10,159
Pretty, huh?

488
00:36:10,440 --> 00:36:11,239
Ma Na.

489
00:36:13,159 --> 00:36:15,159
Please remove your nail polish.

490
00:36:16,360 --> 00:36:17,480
No more makeup either.

491
00:36:19,199 --> 00:36:19,920
You control that too?

492
00:36:20,800 --> 00:36:22,079
Offstage, no.

493
00:36:22,840 --> 00:36:25,280
Onstage, everything is my call.

494
00:36:26,320 --> 00:36:29,000
The Little Mermaid cannot wear makeup.

495
00:36:31,119 --> 00:36:31,519
Also,

496
00:36:33,039 --> 00:36:34,800
your English has a heavy accent.

497
00:36:35,840 --> 00:36:37,880
It doesn't suit the Little Mermaid.

498
00:36:39,639 --> 00:36:40,920
Your pronunciation must be flawless.

499
00:36:41,840 --> 00:36:44,280
The Little Mermaid is the lead.

500
00:36:45,239 --> 00:36:46,079
Stay after today

501
00:36:46,519 --> 00:36:48,719
and read every chapter 30 more times.

502
00:36:53,119 --> 00:36:53,920
Mr. Zhou.

503
00:36:54,559 --> 00:36:56,000
May I ask you something?

504
00:36:56,800 --> 00:36:57,320
Of course.

505
00:36:58,760 --> 00:37:00,480
Do you have a problem with me?

506
00:37:02,840 --> 00:37:04,559
I have no problem with anyone.

507
00:37:05,719 --> 00:37:07,239
I'm responsible for my work,

508
00:37:08,199 --> 00:37:09,039
